  "implications": "The findings support the cautious integration of LLMs into systematic review workflows, particularly when high sensitivity is prioritised, such as in initial title/abstract screening. Prompt optimisation and ensemble methods appear essential to achieve reliable performance and should be standardised in future implementations. Further high‑quality, blinded diagnostic studies with consistent reference standards are needed to quantify precision, workload savings, and the impact on downstream review stages. Research should also explore the trade‑off between sensitivity and precision in imbalanced datasets and assess the generalisability of fine‑tuned, domain‑specific models across diverse review topics."
